==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|flint|y}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈflɪnti/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-flinty.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-flinty.wav|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪnti|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# Resembling or containing [[flint]]; [[hard]] like flint.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1973|author=Patsy Adam Smith|authorlink=Patsy Adam-Smith|title=The Barcoo Salute|publisher=Rigby|location=Adelaide|page=2|text=It was late at night and frosty; high above them on the hills the cloppety clop, cloppety clop of a horse's hooves picking their way on the '''flinty''' stone track died away in the distance.}}
# {{lb|en|geology}} [[siliceous|Siliceous]] (including [[basanite]]).
#: {{ux|en|'''flinty''' rock}}
#: {{ux|en|'''flinty''' slate}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Showing a [[lack]] of [[emotion]].
#* {{quote-web|en|url=http://www.theguardian.com/politics/2012/aug/22/britannia-unchained-rise-of-new-tory-right|title=Britannia Unchained: the rise of the new Tory right|date=2012-08-22|author=Andy Beckett|work=The Guardian|passage=Public opinion has turned '''flintier''' in recent years on welfare spending.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|title=Robbie Robertson, 80, Dies; Canadian Songwriter Captured American Spirit|date=2023-08-09|work=The New York Times|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/08/09/arts/music/robbie-robertson-dead.html|passage=While the texture of his playing was often '''flinty''', his licks and leads were flush with feeling.}}
# {{lb|en|wine}} Having a [[taste]] characteristic of certain [[white wine]]s, especially [[Chablis]], supposed to evoke the sensation of flint striking [[steel]].

